// GLOBAL-FACT DISCHARGE — the CONSTANT witness (model-free).
//
// A `forall_elim` over a refined universal `forall h: H` at a CONSTANT `c` owes the guard
// `good(c)`. Here `good(c)` is proven by a GLOBAL AXIOM `goodC` — NOT by any prior step or
// enclosing binder. The discharge must demand + cite that global fact. (This is exactly the
// "constant -> base closure fact" shape a guarded-sort model transfer needs, isolated from
// any model: it is a plain refined-sort proof.)
sort G
pred good(x: G)
sort H = G where good
const c: G
func f(x: G): G

axiom goodC: good(c)              // the global discharge fact for the constant witness
axiom fLaw: forall h: H; f(h) = h // a law over the refined subset

// forall_elim(c) derives `good(c) -> f(c) = c`; the guard good(c) must discharge from
// `goodC` (global) so the step claims bare `f(c) = c`. No prior `good(c)` step is written —
// the discharge finds the global axiom itself.
theorem fAtConst: f(c) = c
proof
  @the-law |
    forall h: H; f(h) = h
    [by axiom fLaw]
  @conclusion |
    f(c) = c
    [by forall_elim(c) the-law]
qed
